      "writtenOn": "2026-05-19T20:43:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "These two descriptions don\u0027t really help me understand the new feature. I would suggest not bothering to mention the existing feature if you aren\u0027t altering it, unless you are going to describe how the new feature interacts with the old feature. Some things to consider, what happens in your example below if those two items are defined under the same project section, and what happens if they are defined in different project sections? I think we definitely want test cases to cover both those situations. I suspect currently if they are defined in the same project section, that this will reserve a total of 7 slots, but I am not sure that is what it should do? Should it instead reserve 5 for the project as a whole, and within those 5, should 2 be reserved for receivepacks leaving only 3 reserved for all other operations for that project? @achakilam@nvidia.com any recommendations here?",
      "revId": "42c392a91d78347ece1e0e9849b13d2c6df16001",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9efb90d0_1326af6b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 4069542
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-05-20T23:40:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think about each quota individually. There shouldn\u0027t be a relation between them (at least not documented behaviour). Considering the existing max starts:\n\n```\n[quota project]\n  maxStartForTaskForQueue \u003d 5 receivepack SSH-Interactive-Worker\n  maxStartForTaskForUserForQueue \u003d 2 receivepack user SSH-Interactive-Worker\n```\n\nWe do have a hard max of 5 not 7 here. The maxStart makes it look as if we are following some hierarchy between those quota rules but we are still treating each quota individually.\n\nTo remove such confusion for minStart, I think we should just migrate the existing `minStartForQueue` to `minStartForTaskForQueue`. We could still achieve it by doing the following:\n\n```\n[quota project]\n  minStartForTaskForQueue \u003d 3 ^.*$ SSH-Interactive-Worker\n  minStartForTaskForQueue \u003d 2 receivepack SSH-Interactive-Worker\n```",
      "parentUuid": "3a479cdc_aa7ae082",
      "revId": "42c392a91d78347ece1e0e9849b13d2c6df16001",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
